# A Battle ({2}{W}, Invasion of Belenon) is castableAsPermanent too
# (castspell.go lists Battle alongside creature/artifact/enchantment/
# planeswalker). This one stops at the stack rather than resolving all the
# way to the battlefield the way the other four permanent-type fixtures do:
# every Battle in the corpus carries its own "when this enters, create a
# token" trigger (CR 603.2), and checkETBTriggers (trigger.go) now correctly
# detects and pushes it the moment permanentEffect moves the Battle onto the
# battlefield -- but Token is one of the 203 corpus-frequency effects M6
# still owns, so resolvestack would surface ErrUnimplemented rather than
# leaving a clean state for expect.state to describe. TestScenarios has no
# way to assert an expected RunActions failure, so that half of the picture
# is proven at the engine level instead (TestCastSpellFiresETBTrigger,
# trigger_test.go, using a synthetic card of the same shape). This fixture
# stays at what it can show cleanly: the cast itself succeeds and the Battle
# reaches the stack.
startturn human
advance 3
tapformana human 2 W
tapformana human 3 G
tapformana human 4 G
queue paygeneric G
queue paygeneric G
castspell human 1
